This repository is a fork of yakidango-official/GhostLock-H80GT. The exploit
core is unmodified from that project; what a23bc's fork adds is target profiles
measured from the Honor X50's own boot images, plus the verification tooling and
documentation behind them.

There are two stages of authorship here, and they should not be conflated:

  1. a23bc's ALI-AN00 port - the X50 target profiles, the exploit adaptation,
     the ksu/ loader (load_ko.c and the bind-mounted kallsyms approach), and
     docs/ALI-AN00-*.md. This is what the present work was cloned from.

  2. This fork - the KernelSU LKM port under port/ (patch, build, device and
     host tooling, allowlist generator), docs/LKM-PORT.md, the README
     restructure and README.zh-CN.md. A different approach to the same goal: an
     external kernelsu.ko with a runtime symbol shim, instead of ksu/'s
     fake-kallsyms loader.

