ADDED  exploit/src/targets/annap-ALI-AN00_9.0.0.220/target.h
       Honor X50 (ALI-AN00), MagicOS 9.0.0.220, kernel
       5.10.236-android12-9-gf68ed03ce0d2. Kernel-symbol offsets measured from
       the device's own boot image, not copied from another model.

ADDED  exploit/src/targets/annap-ALI-TN00_9.0.0.230/target.h
       Honor X50 (ALI-TN00), MagicOS 9.0.0.230, kernel
       5.10.236-android12-9-g4b262e5255ed. Same method.

       Both profiles inherit struct-layout offsets (FAKE_TASK_*, WAITER_*,
       TASK_CRED_OFF, MM_OWNER_OFF, and the random_table + 0x100 boot_id entry)
       from the upstream 80 GT profile. Those are NOT verified on either X50
       device; each is flagged inline in the target.h files.

ADDED  docs/ALI-AN00-TN-COMPARISON.md    two-boot symbol diff, build verification
ADDED  docs/ALI-AN00-VERIFICATION.md     offset provenance and what stays unproven
ADDED  docs/ALI-AN00-SYMBOLS.txt         measured symbol table and kernel config
ADDED  docs/cmp_boots.py                 reproducible two-boot symbol comparison
ADDED  docs/verify_offsets.py            reproducible profile-offset check

CHANGED  exploit/Makefile
       Default PROJECT switched from the 80 GT profile to the X50 one. The NDK
       host tag is now detected instead of hardcoded to prebuilt/linux-x86_64,
       which on a Windows host pointed --sysroot at a nonexistent path and made
       every libc include fail. RESOURCE_DIR is globbed rather than pinned to
       lib/clang/21, which does not exist in NDK r29.

CHANGED  README.md
       Rewritten to cover the Honor X50; per-device tables for other models were
       dropped from it.

NOT CHANGED  ksu/README.md
       Still the Honor 80 GT loader documentation this fork was cloned from. A
       scope note at the top now states that it does not work for the X50, which
       uses port/ instead. An earlier draft of this NOTICE claimed this file had
       been rewritten for the X50; that was wrong, and is corrected here.

ADDED    README.zh-CN.md
       Restored after the earlier English-only pass. README.md is the English
       entry point and links to it; the rest of the repository stays English.

CHANGED  release/setup.sh
       Three runtime prompts translated from Chinese to English.

CHANGED  docs/cmp_boots.py, docs/verify_offsets.py, ksu/build_inner.sh
       Comments and output rewritten in English; no functional change to the
       scripts.

NOT CHANGED  exploit/src/*.c, exploit/src/*.h — the exploit core.

Hardware-tested on ALI-AN00, MagicOS 9.0.0.220 (see README). Firmware version
strings could not be verified from inside the boot images: neither dump contains build.prop, MagicOS, or ALI-* strings.

CHANGED  exploit/src/sysctl.c
       Added a SYSCTL_VERIFY_ONLY pre-flight gate before the cred write. When
       set, the chain stops after the VERIFY stage and reports the measured
       mm->owner / task->comm offsets. Used to prove the profile is correct on a
       device without risking a misdirected cred write.

CHANGED  exploit/src/util.c
       prepare_dm_page(): pages whose perf-oracle physical alias falls outside
       the direct map (observed ~0xc00000000 on this SoC) are now retired
       immediately instead of being silently skipped, and the candidate budget
       went from 16 to 32 rounds. On the X50 the old behaviour burned the whole
       attempt budget on a reading that never changes for that page; this is
       what made runs after the first minute of boot fail consistently.

